# udev/90-dock-lid-holdoff.rules
# ==============================
#
# Hold off logind's lid-switch handling for 30 s whenever anything is plugged
# into a USB-C port, so a lid closed while the Thunderbolt dock is still
# connecting cannot suspend into the half-enumerated dock. On 2026-10-19 that
# suspend hung the laptop until a forced power-off.
#
# The USB-C partner device is the EARLIEST signal a plug-in gives: measured
# 1.8 s before logind reports external power and 3 s before the dock's
# Thunderbolt link. The rule only pulls in dock-lid-holdoff.service, which takes
# the lock; when it lapses logind re-evaluates the still-closed lid itself.
#
# SOURCE OF TRUTH. Copied root-owned to /etc/udev/rules.d/ by
# scripts/setup-dock-lid.sh (never symlinked -- root's udevd reads it). Editing
# this copy changes nothing until `dock-lid-setup` is re-run, and
# `dock-lid-setup --check` reports the difference as drift.
#
# The unit name below must match systemd/dock-lid-holdoff.service: a wrong name
# yields a rule that verifies cleanly and then never fires.
# scripts/test-dock-lid.sh asserts they agree.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="typec", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="typec_partner", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="dock-lid-holdoff.service"
